Body:
## Debug Config Output

```json
{
  "plugin": [
    "oh-my-openagent",
    "@slkiser/opencode-quota",
    "file:///Users/dion.jones/.config/opencode/plugin/cursor-acp.js",
    "list"
  ],
  "provider": {
    "github-copilot": {
      "models": {
        "*": {
          "options": {
            "serviceTier": null
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Verification

Attempted config workaround of setting `serviceTier: null` but **error persists**:

```
task(subagent_type="explore", run_in_background=true, prompt="...")
→ Error: service_tier is not supported
```

## Root Cause Analysis

Setting `serviceTier: null` in provider config **does not prevent the parameter from being sent** - it appears OpenCode still includes `service_tier` in the API request payload (possibly as `service_tier: null`), which GitHub Copilot rejects.

The parameter needs to be **completely omitted** from the request body for GitHub Copilot, not just set to `null`.

## Impact

- All subagent types affected: `explore`, `librarian`, `oracle`, `general`
- Error occurs immediately on subagent spawn
- Blocks all task delegation and agent orchestration
- Main agent (`build`) works fine - only subagents fail

This is reproducible 100% of the time with the current OpenCode 1.15.13 + GitHub Copilot provider combination.
